  "upload": {
    "title": "This SUV Bounces Itself Out of Sand 🤯 #shorts",
    "description": "Mercedes-Benz E-ACTIVE BODY CONTROL is a 48-volt active suspension that controls every wheel on its own. Stuck in a dune? Free-driving mode raises and lowers the body again and again, changing the tyres' ground pressure until they grip and the SUV rocks itself free. It can also scan the road ahead and smooth bumps before you feel them. Plot twist: so few buyers ordered it that Mercedes dropped it from the GLE in the US.",
